---@field state? gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleStateEnum Optional. The mapping rule state
---@field multiColumnDataTypeChange? gcp.datamigration_v1.MultiColumnDatatypeChange Optional. Rule to specify how multiple columns should be converted to a different data type.
---@field conditionalColumnSetValue? gcp.datamigration_v1.ConditionalColumnSetValue Optional. Rule to specify how the data contained in a column should be transformed (such as trimmed, rounded, etc) provided that the data meets certain criteria.
---@field multiEntityRename? gcp.datamigration_v1.MultiEntityRename Optional. Rule to specify how multiple entities should be renamed.
---@field singleEntityRename? gcp.datamigration_v1.SingleEntityRename Optional. Rule to specify how a single entity should be renamed.
---@field revisionCreateTime? string Output only. The timestamp that the revision was created.
---@field filterTableColumns? gcp.datamigration_v1.FilterTableColumns Optional. Rule to specify the list of columns to include or exclude from a table.
---@field ruleScope? gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleRuleScopeEnum Required. The rule scope
---@field entityMove? gcp.datamigration_v1.EntityMove Optional. Rule to specify how multiple entities should be relocated into a different schema.
---@field sourceSqlChange? gcp.datamigration_v1.SourceSqlChange Optional. Rule to change the sql code for an entity, for example, function, procedure.

---A filter defining the entities that a mapping rule should be applied to. When more than one field is specified, the rule is applied only to entities which match all the fields.
---@class gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleFilter
---@field parentEntity? string Optional. The rule should be applied to entities whose parent entity (fully qualified name) matches the given value. For example, if the rule applies to a table entity, the expected value should be a schema (schema). If the rule applies to a column or index entity, the expected value can be either a schema (schema) or a table (schema.table)
---@field entityNamePrefix? string Optional. The rule should be applied to entities whose non-qualified name starts with the given prefix.
---@field entityNameContains? string Optional. The rule should be applied to entities whose non-qualified name contains the given string.
---@field entities? gcp.datamigration_v1.StringList Optional. The rule should be applied to specific entities defined by their fully qualified names.
---@field entityNameSuffix? string Optional. The rule should be applied to entities whose non-qualified name ends with the given suffix.

---@alias gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleList gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRule[]

---@alias gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleRuleScopeEnum "DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_SCHEMA"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_TABLE"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_COLUMN"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_CONSTRAINT"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_INDEX"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_TRIGGER"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_VIEW"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_SEQUENCE"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_STORED_PROCEDURE"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_FUNCTION"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_SYNONYM"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_DATABASE_PACKAGE"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_UDT"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_MATERIALIZED_VIEW"|"DATABASE_ENTITY_TYPE_DATABASE"

---@alias gcp.datamigration_v1.MappingRuleStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ENABLED"|"DISABLED"|"DELETED"

