---Represents a Database Migration Service migration job object.
---@class gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJob
---@field reverseSshConnectivity? gcp.datamigration_v1.ReverseSshConnectivity The details needed to communicate to the source over Reverse SSH tunnel connectivity.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field sourceDatabase? gcp.datamigration_v1.DatabaseType The database engine type and provider of the source.
---@field dumpPath? string The path to the dump file in Google Cloud Storage, in the format: (gs://[BUCKET_NAME]/[OBJECT_NAME]). This field and the "dump_flags" field are mutually exclusive.
---@field filter? string This field can be used to select the entities to migrate as part of the migration job. It uses AIP-160 notation to select a subset of the entities configured on the associated conversion-workspace. This field should not be set on migration-jobs that are not associated with a conversion workspace.
---@field purpose? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobPurposeEnum|string Output only. Migration job mode. Migration jobs can be standard forward jobs or failback migration jobs.
---@field vpcPeeringConnectivity? gcp.datamigration_v1.VpcPeeringConnectivity The details of the VPC network that the source database is located in.
---@field dumpFlags? gcp.datamigration_v1.DumpFlags The initial dump flags. This field and the "dump_path" field are mutually exclusive.
---@field postgresHomogeneousConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.PostgresHomogeneousConfig Optional. Configuration for PostgreSQL homogeneous migration.
---@field staticIpConnectivity? gcp.datamigration_v1.StaticIpConnectivity static ip connectivity data (default, no additional details needed).
---@field postgresToSqlserverConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.PostgresToSqlServerConfig Configuration for heterogeneous failback migrations from **PostgreSQL to SQL Server**.
---@field labels? gcp.datamigration_v1.StringMap The resource labels for migration job to use to annotate any related underlying resources such as Compute Engine VMs. An object containing a list of "key": "value" pairs. Example: `{ "name": "wrench", "mass": "1.3kg", "count": "3" }`.
---@field error? gcp.datamigration_v1.Status Output only. The error details in case of state FAILED.
---@field endTime? string Output only. If the migration job is completed, the time when it was completed.
---@field cmekKeyName? string The CMEK (customer-managed encryption key) fully qualified key name used for the migration job. This field supports all migration jobs types except for: * Mysql to Mysql (use the cmek field in the cloudsql connection profile instead). * PostrgeSQL to PostgreSQL (use the cmek field in the cloudsql connection profile instead). * PostgreSQL to AlloyDB (use the kms_key_name field in the alloydb connection profile instead). Each Cloud CMEK key has the following format: projects/[PROJECT]/locations/[REGION]/keyRings/[RING]/cryptoKeys/[KEY_NAME]
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the migration job resource was created. A timestamp in RFC3339 UTC "Zulu" format, accurate to nanoseconds. Example: "2014-10-02T15:01:23.045123456Z".
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the migration job resource was last updated. A timestamp in RFC3339 UTC "Zulu" format, accurate to nanoseconds. Example: "2014-10-02T15:01:23.045123456Z".
---@field source? string Required. The resource name (URI) of the source connection profile.
---@field originalMigrationName? string Optional. A failback replication pointer to the resource name (URI) of the original migration job.
---@field performanceConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.PerformanceConfig Optional. Data dump and load parallelism settings used by the migration.
---@field duration? string Output only. The duration of the migration job (in seconds). A duration in seconds with up to nine fractional digits, terminated by 's'. Example: "3.5s".
---@field phase? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobPhaseEnum|string Output only. The current migration job phase.
---@field oracleToPostgresConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.OracleToPostgresConfig Configuration for heterogeneous **Oracle to Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL** and **Oracle to AlloyDB for PostgreSQL** migrations.
---@field dumpType? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobDumpTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of the data dump. Supported for MySQL to CloudSQL for MySQL migrations only.
---@field destinationDatabase? gcp.datamigration_v1.DatabaseType The database engine type and provider of the destination.
---@field sqlserverToPostgresConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.SqlServerToPostgresConfig Configuration for heterogeneous **SQL Server to Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL** migrations.
---@field conversionWorkspace? gcp.datamigration_v1.ConversionWorkspaceInfo The conversion workspace used by the migration.
---@field sqlserverHomogeneousMigrationJobConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.SqlServerHomogeneousMigrationJobConfig Optional. Configuration for SQL Server homogeneous migration.
---@field objectsConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobObjectsConfig Optional. The objects that need to be migrated.
---@field state? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobStateEnum|string The current migration job state.
---@field destination? string Required. The resource name (URI) of the destination connection profile.
---@field displayName? string The migration job display name.
---@field name? string The name (URI) of this migration job resource, in the form of: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/migrationJobs/{migrationJob}.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field type? gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobTypeEnum|string Required. The migration job type.
---@field mysqlHomogeneousConfig? gcp.datamigration_v1.MySqlHomogeneousConfig Optional. Configuration for MySQL homogeneous migration.

---@alias gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobDumpTypeEnum "DUMP_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOGICAL"|"PHYSICAL"

---@alias gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJobList gcp.datamigration_v1.MigrationJob[]

