---@field promoteWhenReady? boolean Optional. Promote databases when ready.
---@field useDiffBackup? boolean Optional. Enable differential backups.
---@field backupFilePattern? string Required. Pattern that describes the default backup naming strategy. The specified pattern should ensure lexicographical order of backups. The pattern must define one of the following capture group sets: Capture group set #1 yy/yyyy - year, 2 or 4 digits mm - month number, 1-12 dd - day of month, 1-31 hh - hour of day, 00-23 mi - minutes, 00-59 ss - seconds, 00-59 Example: For backup file TestDB_20230802_155400.trn, use pattern: (?.*)_backup_(?\d{4})(?\d{2})(?\d{2})_(?\d{2})(?\d{2})(?\d{2}).trn Capture group set #2 timestamp - unix timestamp Example: For backup file TestDB.1691448254.trn, use pattern: (?.*)\.(?\d*).trn or (?.*)\.(?\d*).trn

